<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2025-10-13T19:10:14+00:00</updated><id>https://danielmartinruiz.com/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>Hey! I&apos;m Dani, check out my page to see my work and get in touch! </subtitle><entry><title type="html">EASP Summer School 2025</title><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2025/summer_school/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="EASP Summer School 2025"/><published>2025-08-04T09:30:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-08-04T09:30:00+00:00</updated><id>https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2025/summer_school</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2025/summer_school/"><![CDATA[<h2 id="reflecting-on-the-easp-summer-school-2025-in-canterbury">Reflecting on the EASP Summer School 2025 in Canterbury</h2> <p>This summer I had the chance to take part in the <a href="https://blogs.kent.ac.uk/easp2025/thematic-workstreams/">EASP Summer School</a> in Canterbury. It was two weeks full of learning, discussions, and getting to know people from many different places and backgrounds.</p> <p>I joined the <em>Moral Psychology and Artificial Intelligence</em> workstream with <a href="https://www.jimaceverett.com">Jim Everett</a> and <a href="https://www.mgreinecke.com">Madeline (“Gracie”) Reinecke</a>. We looked at AI not just as a technology, but as something that raises deep questions about our values, our decisions, and the way we relate to each other in a world where machines are increasingly present. I found it both challenging and refreshing to think about how psychology, philosophy and AI come together, and how research can engage with these questions in practice.</p> <swiper-container keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/6-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/6-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/6-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/6.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/4.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/5-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/5-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/5-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/5.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2025/1.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container> <p>Outside the classroom, there were plenty of activities that made the experience even richer: from exploring Canterbury to just spending time with others over a meal or during the organized events. Those moments mattered as much as the academic side, because they made it easy to connect, exchange ideas, and feel part of a wider community.</p> <p>Looking back, I’m grateful for the balance of learning, collaboration, and simply sharing experiences. The summer school wasn’t just about the science, but also about the people, the conversations, and the projects that will keep going long after. Thanks to everyone who made this possible.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="psychology"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[2025 Summer School of the European Association of Social Psychology, hosted at the University of Kent]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">PHAIR 2025 in Edinburgh</title><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/phair2025/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="PHAIR 2025 in Edinburgh"/><published>2025-07-15T16:30:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-07-15T16:30:00+00:00</updated><id>https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/edinburgh</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/phair2025/"><![CDATA[<h2 id="the-phair-2025-animal-advocacy-conference-in-edinburgh">The PHAIR 2025 Animal Advocacy Conference in Edinburgh</h2> <p>This July I had the chance to attend <a href="https://phairsociety.org/2025/07/08/phair-2025-conference-an-extraordinary-gathering/">PHAIR 2025</a> in Edinburgh, my very first time at this conference, organized by the <strong>PHAIR Society</strong>. The Society for the Psychology of Human-Animal Intergroup Relations (PHAIR) is an association dedicated to building bridges between psychology and animal advocacy, bringing together researchers, advocates, and practitioners who care about the moral standing of animals and how we should act on it. The conference reflected this mission beautifully: it wasn’t only academics presenting their work, but also activists sharing practical perspectives. That combination made for a unique experience.</p> <p>The setting in Edinburgh couldn’t have been better. The city itself was beautiful, and the atmosphere of the conference was warm, energizing, and incredibly well-organized. I met so many fantastic people. One of the highlights was meeting <a href="https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Singer">Peter Singer</a>, a philosopher whose work has shaped the field for decades. I also had the chance to connect with others whose research has been central to my own, like <a href="https://www.joshuarottman.com">Josh Rottman</a>, <a href="https://www.mattiwilks.com">Matti Wilks</a>, and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/charlie-crimston-4b1229226/?originalSubdomain=au">Charlie Crimston</a>.</p> <swiper-container keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/1.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/2.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/3.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/5-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/5-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/5-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/5.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/4.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/6-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/6-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/6-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/edinburgh2025/6.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container> <p>Overall, PHAIR 2025 was an amazing mix of rigorous discussion and real-world engagement. It was a privilege to be part of a community where psychology and advocacy come together. Can’t wait for the 2027 one!</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="psychology"/><category term="normality"/><category term="morality"/><category term="philosophy"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The PHAIR 2025 Animal Advocacy Conference in Edinburgh]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">5th Euro Xphi Conference in Norwich</title><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2025/norwich/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="5th Euro Xphi Conference in Norwich"/><published>2025-07-15T16:30:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-07-15T16:30:00+00:00</updated><id>https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2025/norwich</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2025/norwich/"><![CDATA[<h2 id="attending-and-presenting-at-the-5th-european-experimental-philosophy-conference">Attending and presenting at the 5th European Experimental Philosophy Conference</h2> <p>Last week I had the chance to attend the <a href="https://x-phi.uea.ac.uk/EuroX-Phi2025-conference/">EuroX-Phi 2025 conference</a> at the University of East Anglia in Norwich. The city itself was a lovely surprise, quiet, beautiful, and full of character, and the atmosphere of the event was just as welcoming. I got to meet some really nice people, exchange ideas informally, and enjoy the feeling of being part of this lifely community working on similar projects.</p> <swiper-container keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/1.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/2.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/3.png" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/4.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/5-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/5-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/5-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/norwich2025/5.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container> <p>The conference also featured some fantastic keynotes, including a talk by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joshua_Knobe">Josh Knobe</a> that sparked a lot of discussion. I presented my own project, <em>Practical Reason: Frequency and Evaluation Effects on Judgments of Normality and Reasonableness</em>, which is part of my broader project on how people think about normality and practical reasoning.</p> <p>It was great to share my work in this setting, get feedback, and see how it connects with other ongoing debates. Overall, it was an inspiring few days, both intellectually and personally.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="psychology"/><category term="normality"/><category term="morality"/><category term="philosophy"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The 5th edition of the European Experimental Philosophy Conference]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">2025 BioXPhi Summit in Basel</title><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/basel2025/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="2025 BioXPhi Summit in Basel"/><published>2025-07-01T15:30:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-07-01T15:30:00+00:00</updated><id>https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/basel2025</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/basel2025/"><![CDATA[<h2 id="attending-and-presenting-at-the-2025-bioxphi-summit-in-basel">Attending and presenting at the 2025 BioXPhi Summit in Basel</h2> <p>I recently attended the <a href="https://ibmb.unibas.ch/en/public-outreach/projects-to-the-public/basel-oxford-nus-bioxphi-summit-2025/">2025 Basel-Oxford-NUS BioXPhi Summit</a>, and it was an incredible experience. Held from June 26–27 at the University of Basel, the summit brought together researchers from around the world to explore the emerging field of <em>Bioxphi</em>, where philosophy, moral psychology, and bioethics intersect.</p> <p>The sessions were fascinating, and I particularly enjoyed meeting <a href="https://www.mattiwilks.com">Matti Wilks</a>, whose work on the moral circle and animal ethics has greatly influenced my PhD project.</p> <swiper-container keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/4.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/3.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/basel2025/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/basel2025/1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container> <p>Basel itself was stunning. The city, the river, and its historic streets made for a beautiful backdrop to the summit.</p> <p>Overall, the summit was a perfect combination of learning, discussion, and informal networking. I’m very grateful to the organizers, speacilly <a href="https://ibmb.unibas.ch/en/persons/christian-rodriguez/cv-of-christian-rodriguez/">Christian Rodriguez Perez</a> for creating such a thoughtful and well-run event, and to everyone I met for sharing their ideas. It was a great reminder of how exciting this new area of research is and how much there is to learn.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="psychology"/><category term="animals"/><category term="morality"/><category term="philosophy"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The 2025 edition of the Experimental philosophical bioethics ("BioXPhi") Summit]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Vienna Summer School 2024</title><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2024/summer_school_2/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Vienna Summer School 2024"/><published>2024-10-03T09:30:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-10-03T09:30:00+00:00</updated><id>https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2024/summer_school_2</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2024/summer_school_2/"><![CDATA[<h2 id="stratégies-numériques-pour-la-formation-doctorale-en-sciences-humaines-et-sociales">Stratégies numériques pour la formation doctorale en sciences humaines et sociales</h2> <p>Organised by <a href="https://forschung.univie.ac.at/en/services/research-news/details-en/news/2nd-summer-school-of-the-erasmus-project-raqmyat/">UNIMED and the University of Vienna</a>, this second summer school took place within the <a href="https://www.raqmyatproject.eu/">Erasmus+ project RAQMYAT</a> (“Digital Strategies for Doctoral Training in the Humanities and Social Sciences”). It ran online from 17 to 20 September 2024 and continued in person in Vienna from 23 to 27 September 2024.</p> <p>Throughout the week, we explored how digital tools and experimental methods can enrich research in the humanities. Workshops on data management, online collaboration, and digital analysis opened new ways of thinking about my own work. I realised how much philosophical research can benefit from engaging with digital humanities and psychology, especially when studying moral reasoning and human moral behaviour.</p> <p>The group brought together researchers from across the Mediterranean and beyond, creating a lovely space for exchange and collaboration. Vienna, perhaps the most beautiful city I’ve been to, provided the perfect backdrop for such an inspiring week. Outside the sessions, sharing meals and discovering Vienna together made the experience even more rewarding. Those informal moments turned discussions into friendships and ideas into possible projects.</p> <swiper-container keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/1.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/4-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/4-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/4-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/4.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/3-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/3-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/3-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/3.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/2-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/2-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/2-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_2/2.jpg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container> <p>At the end of the week, <b>I was honoured with the Best Research Poster Award</b>, a recognition that reflected both the effort put into my project and the collaborative spirit that defined the entire week.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="psychology"/><category term="philosophy"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[2024 Summer School of RAQMYAT Project in Vienna, Austria, organized by the UNIMED and the University of Vienna.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Hejnice Summer School 2024</title><link href="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2024/summer_school_1/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Hejnice Summer School 2024"/><published>2024-07-23T09:30:00+00:00</published><updated>2024-07-23T09:30:00+00:00</updated><id>https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2024/summer_school_1</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://danielmartinruiz.com/blog/2024/summer_school_1/"><![CDATA[<h2 id="memories-of-the-2024-summer-school-in-hejnice">Memories of the 2024 Summer School in Hejnice</h2> <p>Organised by the <a href="https://vepss.eu/hejnice/">University of Pardubice</a> (Czech Republic) in collaboration with partner institutions from the Visegrad region, the summer school took place in Hejnice, Czech Republic, from 3 to 7 June 2024 (four days in person and six online).</p> <p>Through lectures, workshops, and field visits, we explored topics such as posthumanism, decolonial ecology, and environmental responsibility. The visit to the nearby Turów mine, one of the largest lignite mines in the Czech-Polish-German border area, was particularly insightful. Its legal, social, and ethical implications illustrated the practical relevance of philosophical research in understanding environmental conflicts and cross-border governance.</p> <swiper-container keyboard="true" navigation="true" pagination="true" pagination-clickable="true" pagination-dynamic-bullets="true" rewind="true"> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/6.JPG" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/6.JPG" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/3.JPG" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/3.JPG" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/4.JPG" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/4.JPG" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/5.JPG" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/5.JPG" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/2.JPG" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/2.JPG" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> <swiper-slide> <figure> <picture> <source class="responsive-img-srcset" srcset="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/1-480.webp 480w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/1-800.webp 800w,/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/1-1400.webp 1400w," type="image/webp" sizes="95vw"/> <img src="/assets/img/blog/summer_school2024_1/1.jpeg" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1 img-small" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" onerror="this.onerror=null; $('.responsive-img-srcset').remove();"/> </picture> </figure> </swiper-slide> </swiper-container> <p>Outside the seminars, the setting in monastery of Hejnice, surrounded by forests and mountains, offered time for reflection and exchange in a more informal way. Shared meals, evening discussions, and small excursions helped create a sense of community and openness that complemented the academic work. These moments were just as valuable as the lectures themselves, fostering genuine dialogue and future and longlasting friendships.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="psychology"/><category term="philosophy"/><category term="environment"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[2024 Summer School of Environmental Philosophy in Hejnice, Czech Republic organized by the University of Pardubice.]]></summary></entry></feed>